diff --git a/HEGEL_REPORT.md b/HEGEL_REPORT.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1eabfed
--- /dev/null
+++ b/HEGEL_REPORT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,151 @@
+# Hegel Property-Based Testing Report: fancy-regex
+
+Target: `fancy-regex` 0.18.0 (commit d00f0f7, main), a regex engine with a
+backtracking VM for lookaround/backreferences that delegates plain patterns to
+the `regex`-crate machinery (`regex-automata`).
+
+Setup: `cargo add --dev hegeltest --ignore-rust-version` (hegeltest 0.28.2
+requires rustc 1.86; the crate pins `rust-version = "1.66"`, so the dev-dep
+raises the effective MSRV for running tests — upstreaming would need
+maintainer sign-off). The existing quickcheck dev-dependency was fully ported
+and removed (its only use was one property in `src/vm.rs`).
+
+## Properties tested
+
+Shared generators live in `tests/common/mod.rs`:
+
+- `draw_plain_pattern(tc, allow_anchors)` — builds *syntactically valid by
+  construction* patterns restricted to the plain-regex subset both engines
+  accept: literals (escaped), `.`/`\d`/`\w`/`\s` classes, bracket classes
+  with ranges and negation, capturing/non-capturing/flag groups
+  (`(?i:` `(?s:` `(?m:`), greedy+lazy quantifiers (`* + ? {m} {m,n} {m,}`),
+  alternation (incl. empty branches), optional anchors `^ $ \b \B`.
+- `draw_fancy_pattern(tc)` — layers fancy features on top, sequentially so
+  backreferences only ever refer to already-closed groups: lookaround
+  (all four kinds), atomic groups `(?>...)`, named groups, numbered `\1` and
+  named `\k<name>` backrefs (wrapped `(?:\1)` so a following digit can't
+  extend the number).
+- `draw_haystack(tc)` — strings over the pattern-literal alphabet (so matches
+  actually occur; measured 71/100 cases reach the matched branch) plus ~10%
+  arbitrary Unicode codepoints.
+
+Properties (one test per property):
+
+1. **`prop_plain_subset_is_match_agrees_with_regex_crate`** (tests/matching.rs)
+   — crown differential: on the plain subset, `fancy_regex::Regex::is_match`
+   must equal `regex::Regex::is_match`, both on the delegation path and with
+   the backtracking VM forced via a no-op `(?=[\s\S]?)` prefix.
+2. **`prop_plain_subset_find_agrees_with_regex_crate`** (tests/finding.rs)
+   — same differential for the exact `find` span (delegate + forced VM).
+3. **`prop_plain_subset_captures_agree_with_regex_crate`** (tests/captures.rs)
+   — same differential for match presence, group count and every group span.
+   The VM-path comparison is one-sided on group *count* (see finding 2).
+4. **`prop_compile_never_panics`** (tests/matching.rs) — `Regex::new` and
+   `Expr::parse_tree` on arbitrary text *and* on valid generated patterns
+   corrupted by random metacharacter insertions (supplements
+   `fuzz/fuzz_targets/fuzz_parser.rs`, which only covers `parse_tree`).
+5. **`prop_match_never_panics`** (tests/matching.rs) — for any compiling
+   pattern (75% generator-valid fancy patterns) and arbitrary haystack,
+   `is_match`/`find`/`captures`/`find_iter` return `Ok`/`Err`, never panic,
+   across backtrack limits {1, 1000, 100000}.
+6. **`prop_backtrack_limit_errors_instead_of_hanging`** (tests/matching.rs)
+   — generated catastrophic patterns `(c+c+)+(?>d)` on `c^n` (n in 12..=40)
+   with `backtrack_limit(1000)`, `seek(false)` must return
+   `RuntimeError::BacktrackLimitExceeded`, not hang (process-abort/hang class).
+7. **`prop_escape_then_match_roundtrip`** (tests/matching.rs) —
+   `Regex::new(escape(text))` compiles and finds exactly `(0, text.len())`
+   on `text`, for arbitrary Unicode text.
+8. **`prop_find_iter_spans_wellformed`** (tests/finding.rs) — with full fancy
+   features: spans in bounds, on char boundaries, non-overlapping, in order,
+   never the same span twice, and the first item equals `find`.
+9. **`prop_matched_text_rematches_anchored`** (tests/finding.rs) — for
+   anchor-free plain patterns, the matched substring re-matches
+   `^(?:pattern)$` in isolation (matching is context-free).
+10. **`prop_captures_group0_equals_find`** (tests/captures.rs) — for fancy
+    patterns, `captures` group 0 span equals the `find` span.
+11. **`state_save_hegel`** (src/vm.rs) — port of the existing quickcheck model
+    test: VM `State` save slots behave like a stack of snapshots under
+    arbitrary push/pop/save sequences (up to 100 ops, drawn size).
+12. **`prop_capture_names_never_panics_known_failure`** (tests/captures.rs)
+    — KNOWN FAILURE pin for bug 1 below; deliberately failing.
+
+## Test results
+
+- Full suite at default counts: everything passes except the deliberate pin
+  (12 hegel tests; 1 pinned failure, deterministic — fails every case).
+- Liveness verified: temporarily inverting the find-differential assertion
+  produced a fully shrunk counterexample (`pattern="" hay=""`); guarded
+  branches measured live (rematch guard hit 71/100 cases; oracle compile
+  failures are rare enough that no FilterTooMuch health check fires).
+- Exploratory 10x run (`test_cases = 1000` on all properties, then reverted):
+  found finding 2 below on `prop_plain_subset_captures_agree_with_regex_crate`
+  (`(){0}` on `""`); after scoping the VM-path group-count comparison, the
+  full 10x run is green.
+
+## Suspected bugs
+
+1. **Panic in `Regex::capture_names()` for delegated patterns with a named
+   group repeated `{0}`** — real bug, pinned by
+   `prop_capture_names_never_panics_known_failure` (left failing).
+   `fancy_regex::Regex::new("(?<n>a){0}").unwrap().capture_names()` panics
+   with `index out of bounds: the len is 1 but the index is 1` at
+   src/lib.rs:1643. Root cause: regex-syntax elides the `{0}` group from the
+   delegated program, so `captures_len()` == 1, but fancy-regex's own parse
+   recorded `named_groups["n"] == 1`; `capture_names()` resizes a Vec to
+   `captures_len()` then writes `names[1]`. Compile succeeds, the panic is in
+   an ordinary accessor — an API-contract violation (the crate returns
+   `Result` everywhere else). Related quieter symptom on the same root cause:
+   `Captures::name("n")` silently returns `None` even though the pattern
+   names the group.
+
+2. **Capture-group count depends on the execution path for `{0}` groups**
+   (semantic divergence, documented rather than pinned): `(a){0}` via
+   delegation reports 1 group (regex-syntax elides the group — the `regex`
+   crate itself reports `captures_len() == 1`), while the same subpattern on
+   the VM path (e.g. `(?=x?)(a){0}`) reports 2 groups with group 1 unset
+   (PCRE-like). Since the oracle (`regex`) is the party deviating from PCRE
+   semantics here, the differential's VM-path group-count check was made
+   one-sided (extra VM-side groups must be unset) instead of pinning fancy as
+   buggy. Worth an upstream conversation because it makes group numbering
+   pattern-path-dependent, and it is the same elision that causes bug 1.
+
+3. **Compile-compatibility divergence: `(?:)*`, `(?i:)?`, `(?:){2}` etc. are
+   rejected** (`ParseError::TargetNotRepeatable`) while the `regex` crate
+   accepts them all, and fancy itself accepts `()*` and `(?:|)*`. This is
+   deliberate-looking (`is_repeatable()` returns false for `Expr::Empty`,
+   with an Oniguruma-mode carve-out that *skips* the quantifier), so it is
+   reported as a divergence, not pinned: patterns valid for the regex crate
+   fail to compile on fancy-regex outside Oniguruma mode. The plain-pattern
+   generator marks empty non-capturing/flag groups non-quantifiable, with a
+   comment pointing here.
+
+## Unsound properties abandoned
+
+- **Exact VM-path captures equality vs the regex crate** — weakened to the
+  one-sided group-count comparison after finding 2; asserting equality with
+  the oracle's `{0}`-elision behavior would assert something fancy-regex
+  never promised (and arguably shouldn't do).
+- **"fancy accepts everything regex accepts"** (implicit in the first draft
+  of the differential generators) — false per finding 3; the generator was
+  constrained (empty `(?:)` not quantified) rather than asserting it.
+- The VM-forced differentials tolerate `BacktrackLimitExceeded` (generated
+  plain patterns can be catastrophic, e.g. `(a*)*` shapes, and the VM's
+  documented limit applies); property 6 covers that contract explicitly.
+
+## Skill feedback
+
+- The Oracle Sourcing guidance ("dispatcher's generic fallback vs specialized
+  fast path") mapped perfectly here: the delegation path is nearly-tautological
+  as a differential, but forcing the backtracking VM with a semantics-neutral
+  `(?=[\s\S]?)` prefix turned the same oracle into a real cross-engine check.
+  A sentence about "force the slow path with a no-op wrapper" might be worth
+  adding to the catalogue.
+- The 10x exploratory run earned its keep exactly as documented: `(){0}` did
+  not appear in 100-case runs but did at 1000, and shrinking produced the
+  minimal counterexample immediately.
+- Sequential (imperative) generation made valid-backref construction trivial
+  (generate left-to-right, only reference closed groups) — this would be
+  painful in declarative PBT frameworks and is a good showcase pattern.
+- One friction point: `eprintln!`-based vacuity counting requires
+  `-- --nocapture`, which is easy to forget since passing hegel tests print
+  nothing; a note in the reference's liveness section would help.
